630bb493ebb9e55c102a53b829091e95943ed914d076353f02534c67e3df2","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"scripts/scroll.py","size":676,"sha256":"17e11b0653e5520b2a4de7897580be71f35d366a52a79776f6422d9c600fecde","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"scripts/type_text.py","size":513,"sha256":"b75112b6c475615b34dd334432388a00883c053d1d7afa0719624c54929add30","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"scripts/wait_for_text.py","size":1607,"sha256":"13c8fee3891f40d26d95207e17a2ba7cbef6fe89c4834f0ec51f6b4c8bff0ef5","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"scripts/wait_for_window.py","size":1099,"sha256":"05795ea9a89c9409f9a04e0f61c554dfe2378ff86bf10b4a055f142a223c8c4b","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2104,"sha256":"0f014023feae9225d2f6923e86acfdd4e875b2d58fc4f17008c7230bcbb3c7e2","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789027552335,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"5d464d7c9afc9bb891062615ea2489b7ca37428c49c50770c2da0e70f6bb6317","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/5d464d7c9afc9bb891062615ea2489b7ca37428c49c50770c2da0e70f6bb6317","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: windows-control\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThis skill is classified as suspicious due to its inherently high-risk capabilities, which include full Windows desktop control, reading content from any open window (including browsers and dialogs), simulating mouse and keyboard input, and taking screenshots. While these actions are explicitly documented and aligned with the skill's stated purpose of 'Full Windows desktop control' in SKILL.md, they grant extensive access to sensitive user data and system interaction. There is no evidence of intentional malicious behavior such as data exfiltration to external endpoints, persistence mechanisms, or obfuscation within the Python scripts. The SKILL.md also lacks prompt-injection attempts to subvert the agent's instructions for malicious purposes. However, the broad permissions and ability to interact with and extract information from any application make it a powerful tool that could be easily misused, thus warranting a 'suspicious' classification rather than 'benign'.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160777135},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":81,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":32,"checkedAt":1789027552335},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill openly provides broad Windows desktop control, but its unrestricted clicks, keystrokes, screen reading, and dialog actions need careful review before use.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Full desktop control is high-impact and not scoped to approved apps, windows, regions, or safe action types, so a mistaken invocation could expose sensitive visible data or perform unintended UI actions.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The package metadata includes only SKILL.md and local scripts; I found no install hook, remote payload retrieval, or hidden setup behavior in the inspected artifacts.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The documentation encourages acting across any Windows application, including clicking by loose text match, closing windows by partial title, and dismissing dialogs, without strong warnings, confirmation steps, exact-target requirements, or privacy guidance for captured screen/UI content.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The inspected scripts do not create persistence, modify agent memory, install services, use credential stores, or request privilege escalation; actions run in the user's current GUI session.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is full Windows desktop automation, and the inspected scripts implement that with mouse clicks, typing, hotkeys, screenshots, UI text extraction, browser/window reading, window management, and dialog handling.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you intentionally want an agent to control and read your Windows desktop. Use it in a controlled session, prefer listing/reading windows before acting, avoid sensitive apps or visible secrets, and require explicit human confirmation before clicks, hotkeys, closing windows, saving, accepting, deleting, or dismissing dialogs.","findings":"[TP4] expected: Downgraded for the whole package: individual scripts are narrow modules, but together they implement the advertised mouse, keyboard, screenshot, window, browser, and dialog automation capabilities.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: Accepted in substance: the powerful desktop actions are disclosed and purpose-aligned, but the artifacts lack adequate safety boundaries for destructive confirmations, arbitrary clicks/keystrokes, broad screen capture, and sensitive UI text extraction.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789027552335}}}}}